{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792312279,"nonce":"gEeYZbpOVh6jPrNHQKXOOAGzDS8=","title":"Real apps in a page: files read at run time, and a scene or app with no environment","message":"The banner scene (a glTF car, canvas gauges, an OpenStreetMap extract, glass panels, motion) is the first real demo to run in a browser through Ash's wasm target. This tracks what it needed in the library, and what is still open.\n\n**Done**\n\n- A page has no files and no environment variables. `ashui.core.Assets` gives a file's bytes or text by its path, or what the build embedded under that path (`Assets.embed(directory, ?path)`, a compiler macro); `Bitmap.load`, `Fonts.load`, `Gltf.load`, `Css.loadFile` and `ThemeBundle.withCssFile` read through it. A scene opens as a window in a page without `ASHUI_WINDOW` being set; the banner plays live in a window, its clock driven by the animation scheduler.\n- Memory: the page's shared memory is capped at 1 GiB by Ash, and 512 MB of it is taken before `main` runs. A 4096 by 4096 texture's levels were each sent whole (see the texture issue).\n- Pipeline compilation: Chrome on macOS never finished the liquid glass pipeline (see the glass issue).\n- The generated WebGPU agent passed `undefined` for an optional argument and `setBindGroup` stopped working after some seconds (x-idl 030b19e).\n\n**Open**\n\n- Pins: x-idl, xgpu and hlwgpu need the x-idl fix before a page built from released packages has it.\n- Ash: a native of xwindow.wasm called from a thread throws (Ash 191b6e9); the generated page has no way to hide its log (Ash 7f353ef); the first 512 MB of memory.\n- The page itself, how an app builds for the web from released packages, and a lane check that runs the banner.","files":null}]}